00:00:00,010 --> 00:00:04,930
[ Watch on kissFlix.co ]

1
00:00:05,208 --> 00:00:07,480
- Previously…
- I’m friends with a Kongpurim. So what, Dad?

2
00:00:07,730 --> 00:00:09,960
You said it was grown-up business, didn’t you?

3
00:00:10,031 --> 00:00:11,200
So it has nothing to do with a kid like me.

4
00:00:12,760 --> 00:00:15,261
I’m stressed because there’s something I want to do,

5
00:00:15,280 --> 00:00:16,400
but I know my family would never approve.

6
00:00:16,630 --> 00:00:19,440
Then just do it without letting them find out. It’s that simple.

7
00:00:21,454 --> 00:00:22,800
I think I like you, Blue.

8
00:00:24,560 --> 00:00:27,920
And I never want our time together to end.

9
00:01:04,860 --> 00:01:06,861
[Blue: Where are you?]

10
00:01:11,900 --> 00:01:14,901
[Tokyo: I've been waiting for you, please hurry.]

11
00:02:00,140 --> 00:02:01,780
[Look at what's stuck under the table.]

12
00:02:13,340 --> 00:02:15,341
[Share it with someone you like.]

13
00:02:19,330 --> 00:02:20,650
- Tokyo.
- Tokyo.

14
00:02:36,021 --> 00:02:37,022
Oh, hey.

15
00:02:38,570 --> 00:02:39,571
Hey.

16
00:02:43,090 --> 00:02:44,730
- Hey.
- Yeah?

17
00:02:45,680 --> 00:02:48,773
Are you okay? Why are you smiling like that?

18
00:02:49,150 --> 00:02:51,151
I'm fine. It's nothing.

19
00:02:52,074 --> 00:02:53,285
Nothing?

20
00:02:53,946 --> 00:02:56,330
I've seen you staring at your phone for weeks now.

21
00:02:56,832 --> 00:02:58,570
Nothing.

22
00:02:58,915 --> 00:03:01,130
I was just checking the trending hashtags.

23
00:03:03,357 --> 00:03:05,770
Yeah, whatever. If there's nothing, then there's nothing.

24
00:03:07,490 --> 00:03:09,350
Hey, this evening

25
00:03:09,760 --> 00:03:12,410
my band has rehearsal . We're practicing a new song. Wanna come watch?

26
00:03:12,554 --> 00:03:13,810
- Sure.
- This evening?

27
00:03:14,980 --> 00:03:16,050
I need to go to the library.

28
00:03:16,770 --> 00:03:17,771
- What?
- Huh?

29
00:03:18,381 --> 00:03:19,690
- What for?
- Yeah.

30
00:03:21,382 --> 00:03:22,650
I have to work on the display board,

31
00:03:24,749 --> 00:03:26,210
so you two can go to the rehearsal room without me.

32
00:03:27,421 --> 00:03:28,422
I'm gonna head out.

33
00:03:29,106 --> 00:03:30,107
What?

34
00:03:30,349 --> 00:03:31,370
Tokyo?

35
00:03:31,950 --> 00:03:32,951
What's wrong with her?

36
00:04:06,928 --> 00:04:08,050
Where are Jai and Pupay?

37
00:04:08,832 --> 00:04:11,410
You three are practically inseparable.

38
00:04:13,218 --> 00:04:14,219
Why'd you ask?

39
00:04:16,797 --> 00:04:17,970
Are you jealous?

40
00:04:18,293 --> 00:04:21,810
Oh, please. Who would be that stupid?

41
00:04:23,258 --> 00:04:25,890
Jai and Pupay are pretty much the only friends I have.

42
00:04:26,840 --> 00:04:27,841
When we were kids,

43
00:04:28,050 --> 00:04:31,250
other parents wouldn't let their kids play with kids like me.

44
00:04:32,610 --> 00:04:33,611
You know why?

45
00:04:34,237 --> 00:04:36,210
Because if they ever hurt me,

46
00:04:37,010 --> 00:04:38,570
my dad would...

47
00:04:42,664 --> 00:04:43,850
You just left like that.

48
00:04:44,565 --> 00:04:45,810
Didn't they get suspicious?

49
00:04:48,005 --> 00:04:49,006
Well…

50
00:04:49,669 --> 00:04:51,250
Yeah, they were suspicious.

51
00:04:51,941 --> 00:04:52,942
But...

52
00:04:53,872 --> 00:04:55,550
I just kept rambling to cover it up.

53
00:05:04,410 --> 00:05:06,325
Here, a privacy screen protector.

54
00:05:07,386 --> 00:05:10,586
Now we're good. No one can see what we're talking about anymore.

55
00:05:19,973 --> 00:05:22,425
If it's stressing you out this much,

56
00:05:23,125 --> 00:05:24,660
why not just tell everyone?

57
00:05:28,818 --> 00:05:29,819
I can't.

58
00:05:31,304 --> 00:05:34,400
I can't tell them. I know what things are like at home.

59
00:05:36,850 --> 00:05:39,350
If I tell them, it'll probably cause problems.

60
00:05:40,362 --> 00:05:43,570
I don't know what to do either.

61
00:05:47,824 --> 00:05:50,610
มาพบครูที่ห้องธุรการ ด่วน

62
00:06:54,650 --> 00:06:58,330
Attention, please. Ms. Phakjira Monchaitrakul from Class 6/3,

63
00:06:58,490 --> 00:07:00,650
please report to the administration office immediately.

64
00:07:23,290 --> 00:07:24,810
Phakjira, have a seat.

65
00:07:31,402 --> 00:07:33,090
Phakjira and Piyathida,

66
00:07:33,386 --> 00:07:36,850
both of you can pack up all your belongings by this afternoon and move out.

67
00:07:41,840 --> 00:07:42,841
Why did you

68
00:07:43,402 --> 00:07:45,690
suddenly ask us to leave the dorm?

69
00:07:46,370 --> 00:07:48,371
[Request to Leave the Chantrawattana School Dormitory]

70
00:07:49,290 --> 00:07:52,050
Did we do something wrong?

71
00:07:56,100 --> 00:08:00,350
I'm the one who asked them to move you and Pakkard out of the dorm.

72
00:08:00,810 --> 00:08:02,450
So we can live together.

73
00:08:07,490 --> 00:08:10,370
I have to work at the port here,

74
00:08:11,034 --> 00:08:12,035
so I have…

75
00:08:12,429 --> 00:08:14,725
- already bought us a new house--
- Without asking me?

76
00:08:17,682 --> 00:08:19,350
I want to stay in the school dorm with my friends.

77
00:08:19,842 --> 00:08:21,100
I don't want to live at home.

78
00:08:27,778 --> 00:08:28,779
Miss Vee,

79
00:08:30,136 --> 00:08:31,850
I reall like the dorm here.

80
00:08:34,750 --> 00:08:36,251
I’d rather stay here, please.

81
00:08:38,950 --> 00:08:39,951
Blue.

82
00:08:56,434 --> 00:08:57,770
Can't we just talk nicely?

83
00:08:58,277 --> 00:08:59,570
It's always the same.

84
00:09:00,650 --> 00:09:02,970
You never ask me if I'm okay with what you decide.

85
00:09:04,330 --> 00:09:07,131
How could living in a dorm be better than living at home?

86
00:09:07,990 --> 00:09:10,290
I didn't raise you to live a difficult life.

87
00:09:10,330 --> 00:09:11,931
I'm not struggling here.

88
00:09:12,509 --> 00:09:15,010
If anything, living at home might be harder for me.

89
00:09:18,328 --> 00:09:19,329
Blue,

90
00:09:19,912 --> 00:09:22,290
your mom and I have supported you all this time.

91
00:09:22,550 --> 00:09:24,320
You wanted to transfer here because of the special admission program,

92
00:09:24,498 --> 00:09:26,750
so I even moved here with you. What more do you want?

93
00:09:29,570 --> 00:09:31,810
You didn't let me come here that easily for no reason.

94
00:09:32,781 --> 00:09:34,570
You were planning to move your business here all along.

95
00:09:37,170 --> 00:09:38,671
If you want me to believe you,

96
00:09:39,400 --> 00:09:40,850
then be honest.

97
00:09:41,762 --> 00:09:43,410
What are you really after in Kongpurim?

98
00:09:51,248 --> 00:09:53,210
All you need to know is that

99
00:09:54,130 --> 00:09:55,850
everything I've done has been for our family. That's all.

100
00:09:56,410 --> 00:09:58,490
Then just keep focusing one your business,

101
00:09:58,970 --> 00:10:00,271
leave me out of this.

102
00:10:00,770 --> 00:10:02,050
And leave my friends out of this.

103
00:10:36,696 --> 00:10:39,330
Did you pressure her into anything?

104
00:10:40,282 --> 00:10:43,370
She may be stubborn, but she's never acted like this before.

105
00:10:45,418 --> 00:10:46,570
I didn't say anything.

106
00:10:50,642 --> 00:10:52,450
Whatever you're planning to do, please do it soon.

107
00:10:53,298 --> 00:10:55,399
I'm worried something bad might happen again, like it did last time.

108
00:11:13,226 --> 00:11:16,650
That's exactly why I came back here, to settle this once and for all.

109
00:11:21,650 --> 00:11:23,250
I won't let something like this happen again.

110
00:11:23,314 --> 00:11:24,610
But I'm worried about her.

111
00:11:27,368 --> 00:11:28,570
Just wait and see.

112
00:11:29,768 --> 00:11:30,950
Once she runs out of money,

113
00:11:31,169 --> 00:11:32,610
she'll come crawling back home on her own.

114
00:11:33,570 --> 00:11:34,970
Maybe then she'll finally realize

115
00:11:35,650 --> 00:11:38,090
how important family is.

116
00:11:39,773 --> 00:11:42,410
What kind of child thinks she can win against her parents?

117
00:11:52,226 --> 00:11:55,410
- You can use my money for now, if you need it.
- [Another cartoon commission.]

118
00:11:57,352 --> 00:11:58,353
I don't think so.

119
00:11:59,885 --> 00:12:02,370
Why not? I don't mind.

120
00:12:03,146 --> 00:12:05,450
I barely spend any money anyway.

121
00:12:08,181 --> 00:12:09,850
I don't want you to think

122
00:12:09,882 --> 00:12:11,883
I'm staying with you because of your money, like your other friends.

123
00:12:13,250 --> 00:12:14,610
I don't think that about you.

124
00:12:18,021 --> 00:12:20,770
I'll save it as a last resort.

125
00:12:32,760 --> 00:12:33,820
When I was a kid,

126
00:12:35,000 --> 00:12:38,210
my dad gave me everything I wanted.

127
00:12:38,573 --> 00:12:39,890
If I wanted something, I got it.

128
00:12:40,517 --> 00:12:43,365
But the problem was, I didn't know how to manage it.

129
00:12:45,666 --> 00:12:47,730
You were like a princess, huh?

130
00:12:49,245 --> 00:12:51,050
Your family gave you everything you wanted.

131
00:12:53,170 --> 00:12:54,450
Except one thing.

132
00:12:57,941 --> 00:12:58,942
What is it?

133
00:13:00,536 --> 00:13:02,090
You can't leave your palace.

134
00:13:10,938 --> 00:13:13,100
If our families ever found out about us,

135
00:13:14,912 --> 00:13:16,810
it'd be a full-on civil war.

136
00:13:21,853 --> 00:13:24,180
We can keep it between us.

137
00:13:30,285 --> 00:13:33,530
Or we could just get out of here.

138
00:13:36,682 --> 00:13:38,050
I'm going anyway.

139
00:13:38,933 --> 00:13:40,900
My dream is

140
00:13:41,248 --> 00:13:43,850
to get into a university in Bangkok through the quota system

141
00:13:44,426 --> 00:13:47,930
and draw or do something related to art.

142
00:13:51,309 --> 00:13:52,310
That's cool.

143
00:13:53,112 --> 00:13:54,810
I've never thought about any of that.

144
00:13:56,290 --> 00:13:57,291
Why's that?

145
00:13:58,450 --> 00:14:01,050
I mean...what do you want to do when you grow up?

146
00:14:06,608 --> 00:14:07,609
It never crossed my mind.

147
00:14:12,296 --> 00:14:14,730
Honestly, growing up,

148
00:14:15,490 --> 00:14:18,491
I just did whatever Dad and Yi told me to.

149
00:14:20,160 --> 00:14:21,450
They picked my school,

150
00:14:22,677 --> 00:14:24,210
sent me to boxing lessons,

151
00:14:25,024 --> 00:14:27,850
and sometimes I'd go to events as Dad's daughter.

152
00:14:30,990 --> 00:14:31,991
You know,

153
00:14:32,470 --> 00:14:35,490
I never even had to think about where I'd go to university.

154
00:14:38,071 --> 00:14:40,000
Dad was going to make me

155
00:14:40,826 --> 00:14:43,130
study here in the province anyway.

156
00:14:47,250 --> 00:14:48,251
But...

157
00:14:51,354 --> 00:14:52,455
then I met you,

158
00:14:58,304 --> 00:15:00,970
and I realized that

159
00:15:01,736 --> 00:15:03,537
dreams don't have to stay in one place.

160
00:15:06,674 --> 00:15:08,210
Am I being a bad influence on you?

161
00:15:08,578 --> 00:15:10,250
Of course not.

162
00:15:12,933 --> 00:15:15,018
I just want to live my own life

163
00:15:15,736 --> 00:15:17,810
without having to do what Dad and Yi tell me.

164
00:15:19,250 --> 00:15:20,651
That alone would make me happy.

165
00:15:24,016 --> 00:15:28,017
Maybe leaving together

166
00:15:28,617 --> 00:15:30,210
could be the answer for both of us.

167
00:15:34,117 --> 00:15:35,770
Are you sure about going away with me?

168
00:15:37,650 --> 00:15:38,651
Yes, I'm sure.

169
00:15:43,550 --> 00:15:44,551
Listen.

170
00:15:45,451 --> 00:15:47,597
Moving away from home and family

171
00:15:48,008 --> 00:15:49,690
is a huge decision.

172
00:15:52,609 --> 00:15:56,130
I don't want you to come with me

173
00:15:56,490 --> 00:15:58,010
only to regret it later.

174
00:15:59,250 --> 00:16:00,901
Please give it some serious thought.

175
00:16:31,320 --> 00:16:33,650
I'm thinking of applying for a scholarship to study abroad.

176
00:16:34,621 --> 00:16:35,622
What?

177
00:16:35,832 --> 00:16:37,133
Where do you want to go?

178
00:16:37,300 --> 00:16:39,301
You can't even look after yourself with us around.

179
00:16:39,994 --> 00:16:42,870
Yeah, you already sneak out past the guards here.

180
00:16:43,888 --> 00:16:45,970
If you actually study abroad, who's to say you won't disappear on us?

181
00:16:46,570 --> 00:16:48,610
I'll make her carry a GPS tracker at all times.

182
00:16:48,871 --> 00:16:49,872
Sounds good, Dad?

183
00:16:53,303 --> 00:16:54,610
Have you decided

184
00:16:55,570 --> 00:16:56,890
which country you want to study in yet?

185
00:17:00,950 --> 00:17:01,951
England.

186
00:17:02,365 --> 00:17:04,170
England? Really?

187
00:17:04,696 --> 00:17:05,850
Since when are you into football?

188
00:17:06,930 --> 00:17:09,890
No, I enjoy reading Shakespeare's works.

189
00:17:11,416 --> 00:17:13,010
He was born in England,

190
00:17:13,752 --> 00:17:17,253
so I want to see his house there for myself.

191
00:17:17,848 --> 00:17:20,970
If that's all, couldn't you just go there on holiday?

192
00:17:24,824 --> 00:17:27,410
But my school offers a scholarship, Dad.

193
00:17:27,773 --> 00:17:29,410
We wouldn't have to pay for it ourselves.

194
00:17:31,474 --> 00:17:33,890
Well, then…

195
00:17:34,375 --> 00:17:35,650
I'll buy you a house there

196
00:17:36,176 --> 00:17:37,550
and send some people to stay with you.

197
00:17:37,933 --> 00:17:40,250
They'll take care of everything you need, around the clock.

198
00:17:40,750 --> 00:17:41,751
How about that?

199
00:17:46,541 --> 00:17:47,942
I was just saying, Dad.

200
00:17:49,690 --> 00:17:53,410
With my grades, I'd be lucky to even get into a university in Bangkok.

201
00:17:54,810 --> 00:17:55,811
Study in Bangkok?

202
00:17:56,600 --> 00:17:57,601
Sure, go ahead.

203
00:17:58,130 --> 00:17:59,490
If it's Bangkok,

204
00:18:00,031 --> 00:18:02,032
I'll buy some land and build you a house.

205
00:18:02,538 --> 00:18:03,810
Once you graduate, we can sell it.

206
00:18:04,250 --> 00:18:07,150
That's not a bad idea. It'd be a property investment too.

207
00:18:11,370 --> 00:18:12,770
It was just a thought, Dad.

208
00:18:14,690 --> 00:18:18,610
I'm not even sure my scores would get me into a university in Bangkok.

209
00:18:19,087 --> 00:18:20,730
They require pretty high scores.

210
00:18:22,410 --> 00:18:23,411
I was only asking.

211
00:18:43,656 --> 00:18:46,890
She's not picking up. Maybe her dad won't let her out.

212
00:18:50,304 --> 00:18:52,410
What's with all the spending lately?

213
00:18:53,146 --> 00:18:54,147
You win the lottery?

214
00:18:54,613 --> 00:18:57,250
Of course not. I'll just borrow some money from Tokyo.

215
00:18:58,776 --> 00:19:02,330
So you're gonna call and wake her up this early on her day off?

216
00:19:02,674 --> 00:19:03,675
That's right.

217
00:19:08,490 --> 00:19:11,170
Hey, I didn't order this one.

218
00:19:11,381 --> 00:19:12,382
I ordered it for you two.

219
00:19:14,714 --> 00:19:15,715
Go on.

220
00:19:17,040 --> 00:19:18,041
Enjoy it.

221
00:19:20,562 --> 00:19:21,608
Umm…Yi.

222
00:19:22,216 --> 00:19:24,970
If it's about this round's lottery payment,

223
00:19:25,064 --> 00:19:28,065
Mom was wondering if she could have until next week.

224
00:19:28,650 --> 00:19:31,770
- She didn't win anything this time.
- Hey, I'm not here about that.

225
00:19:33,696 --> 00:19:35,010
I've got some work for you.

226
00:19:37,141 --> 00:19:38,450
Get it done,

227
00:19:39,210 --> 00:19:41,130
and I'll reduce what your parents owe.

228
00:19:45,370 --> 00:19:46,650
What kind of job?

229
00:19:47,871 --> 00:19:50,690
It's easy.

230
00:19:52,972 --> 00:19:54,443
You girls can handle it.

231
00:19:55,376 --> 00:19:58,410
Just find out who Tokyo's new best friend is.

232
00:19:59,936 --> 00:20:01,730
A friend? Who?

233
00:20:02,197 --> 00:20:04,090
That Monchaitrakul girl.

234
00:20:05,250 --> 00:20:07,890
Someone spotted her with Tokyo at the market, just the two of them.

235
00:20:09,514 --> 00:20:12,050
Find out what they talk about, what they're up to,

236
00:20:12,350 --> 00:20:14,930
and how close they are. I want every detail.

237
00:20:16,235 --> 00:20:17,830
But from what I've seen at school,

238
00:20:17,841 --> 00:20:20,410
they don't seem that close.

239
00:20:20,842 --> 00:20:24,384
I don't think you'll get much out of this.

240
00:20:30,890 --> 00:20:33,851
Then just let me know if you make any progress

241
00:20:33,891 --> 00:20:36,210
or find out anything else.

242
00:20:37,750 --> 00:20:38,751
Okay?

243
00:20:45,378 --> 00:20:48,930
But if I find out you knew something and didn't tell me,

244
00:20:50,998 --> 00:20:52,699
I'll show up at your doorstep.

245
00:20:56,650 --> 00:20:57,651
Got it.

246
00:21:31,470 --> 00:21:32,471
Hey.

247
00:21:34,373 --> 00:21:37,210
Isn't that the character Blue drew for the library board?

248
00:21:37,989 --> 00:21:38,990
Yeah, I know.

249
00:21:41,650 --> 00:21:42,970
[Tokyo: I've figured it out. I'll take a gap year.]

250
00:21:42,990 --> 00:21:43,991
[It'll give me an excuse to find myself. Good idea?]

251
00:21:44,350 --> 00:21:45,750
[Blue: That's your idea? Think again.]

252
00:21:45,950 --> 00:21:47,720
[Tokyo: Hey, I don't have a clear goal like you do.]

253
00:21:47,951 --> 00:21:49,450
[Blue: Take your time. You'll figure it out. I'll help.]

254
00:21:50,210 --> 00:21:51,211
[Blue: Think about what you like doing.]

255
00:21:51,250 --> 00:21:52,251
[Tokyo: Sleeping.]

256
00:21:52,730 --> 00:21:53,731
[Blue: What else do you like?]

257
00:21:54,250 --> 00:21:55,410
[Tokyo: You.]

258
00:21:55,890 --> 00:21:57,391
[Blue: Is this really the time to joke around?]

259
00:21:57,750 --> 00:21:58,810
[Tokyo: Reading novels and comics.]

260
00:21:58,851 --> 00:22:00,252
[Blue: Almost at the library.]

261
00:22:00,352 --> 00:22:01,353
[Tokyo: Me too.]

262
00:22:29,714 --> 00:22:30,715
What?

263
00:22:32,861 --> 00:22:34,210
Didn't you finish with the library's board?

264
00:22:37,453 --> 00:22:39,850
- That's right.
- What are you doing here?

265
00:22:41,610 --> 00:22:43,811
I am…

266
00:22:49,550 --> 00:22:50,551
I…

267
00:22:53,750 --> 00:22:55,610
I'd like to join the literature club.

268
00:22:57,106 --> 00:22:58,107
Really?

269
00:22:59,570 --> 00:23:00,571
That's right.

270
00:23:01,816 --> 00:23:02,970
But that's a good thing.

271
00:23:03,314 --> 00:23:06,650
Maybe Mr. Po would be willing to fund some new books for the library.

272
00:23:08,797 --> 00:23:09,798
You two,

273
00:23:12,736 --> 00:23:14,405
sort these books

274
00:23:14,437 --> 00:23:17,230
by category and put them on the proper shelves.

275
00:23:24,309 --> 00:23:25,310
As for you,

276
00:23:26,058 --> 00:23:29,610
sort these books by category and put them on the right shelves.

277
00:23:29,930 --> 00:23:31,050
Don't mix them up.

278
00:23:33,888 --> 00:23:35,130
All of them?

279
00:23:35,640 --> 00:23:36,641
That's right.

280
00:23:44,750 --> 00:23:45,751
Wait.

281
00:23:46,751 --> 00:23:49,430
Ask Mr. Po to donate some new books too, okay?

282
00:23:51,450 --> 00:23:52,451
Sure.

283
00:23:53,485 --> 00:23:55,110
Don't drop any of them.

284
00:24:15,421 --> 00:24:16,810
♪ To you ♪

285
00:24:18,792 --> 00:24:20,850
♪ The one who means everything to me ♪

286
00:24:22,901 --> 00:24:26,730
♪ I'll be waiting to walk beside you ♪

287
00:24:28,421 --> 00:24:31,010
♪ Our dreams won't be far away ♪

288
00:24:31,986 --> 00:24:33,250
♪ But you ♪

289
00:24:35,370 --> 00:24:39,110
♪ slowly faded away and changed ♪

290
00:24:39,471 --> 00:24:43,250
♪ My journey toward my dreams came to an end ♪

291
00:24:44,930 --> 00:24:47,810
♪ No matter how long it takes ♪

292
00:24:48,602 --> 00:24:50,003
♪ I keep waiting ♪

293
00:24:52,994 --> 00:24:54,295
♪ I’ll be waiting ♪

294
00:24:55,250 --> 00:24:57,810
♪ Though it may be only a dream ♪

295
00:24:58,418 --> 00:25:02,250
♪ Of a better day ♪

296
00:25:03,370 --> 00:25:06,050
♪ When you return to me ♪

297
00:25:06,450 --> 00:25:10,290
♪ There’ll be love and everything we need ♪

298
00:25:10,400 --> 00:25:14,290
♪ There’ll be dreams at the end of the road ♪

299
00:25:14,630 --> 00:25:18,450
♪ There'll be the two of us, walking side by side ♪

300
00:25:21,504 --> 00:25:22,750
♪ To you ♪

301
00:25:23,105 --> 00:25:26,550
♪ Who give love depth ♪

302
00:25:27,072 --> 00:25:31,073
♪ There’ll be dreams at the end of the road ♪

303
00:25:31,373 --> 00:25:35,090
♪ There’ll be love and everything we need ♪

304
00:25:38,194 --> 00:25:39,530
♪ To you ♪

305
00:25:39,570 --> 00:25:43,130
♪ Who give love depth ♪

306
00:25:43,485 --> 00:25:47,330
♪ There’ll be dreams at the end of the road ♪

307
00:25:47,746 --> 00:25:51,650
♪ There'll be the two of us, walking side by side ♪

308
00:25:54,490 --> 00:25:55,491
♪ To you ♪

309
00:25:55,750 --> 00:25:59,530
♪ Who give love depth ♪

310
00:25:59,866 --> 00:26:03,970
♪ There’ll be dreams at the end of the road ♪

311
00:26:04,333 --> 00:26:06,834
♪ You’re the one who made my love... ♪

312
00:26:08,605 --> 00:26:10,750
♪ become real ♪

313
00:26:13,536 --> 00:26:14,537
Hey!

314
00:26:16,293 --> 00:26:18,730
There you are. I've been looking everywhere for you.

315
00:26:18,810 --> 00:26:20,611
I'm sorry. I'm so so sorry.

316
00:26:21,850 --> 00:26:25,051
So, are you serious about studying in England?

317
00:26:26,589 --> 00:26:28,018
I….

318
00:26:28,370 --> 00:26:32,330
Our school doesn't offer a scholarship to study in England

319
00:26:32,350 --> 00:26:33,910
like you told your family.

320
00:26:37,290 --> 00:26:38,890
I don't really want to go, actually.

321
00:26:39,391 --> 00:26:41,810
It's just that some of my friends

322
00:26:41,850 --> 00:26:43,251
who do well in school were going there,

323
00:26:43,376 --> 00:26:44,730
so I wanted to go too.

324
00:26:45,377 --> 00:26:47,378
You wanted to follow your friends there to study?

325
00:26:47,461 --> 00:26:49,157
Oh, dear.

326
00:26:49,370 --> 00:26:50,371
There's no need to go.

327
00:26:50,400 --> 00:26:53,401
Why envy people who get better grades than you?

328
00:26:53,877 --> 00:26:56,090
Your family has so much more for others to envy.

329
00:26:56,224 --> 00:26:58,450
You've clearly got a better start in life than most people.

330
00:26:58,704 --> 00:27:00,656
What's the point of studying in England?

331
00:27:00,714 --> 00:27:01,715
Those students will just come back

332
00:27:01,754 --> 00:27:05,890
and work for wealthy business owners like your family anyway.

333
00:27:07,216 --> 00:27:08,750
I think

334
00:27:09,173 --> 00:27:13,010
you'd be better off thinking about how to take over the family business.

335
00:27:14,250 --> 00:27:17,872
So, what's made you take your studies so seriously lately?

336
00:27:19,850 --> 00:27:21,010
Could it be...

337
00:27:21,210 --> 00:27:23,690
that new girl pressuring you?

338
00:27:25,013 --> 00:27:27,214
Oh, she's not pressuring me.

339
00:27:27,890 --> 00:27:28,891
It's nothing.

340
00:27:30,530 --> 00:27:32,131
- Thanks for asking.
- Sure.

341
00:27:40,950 --> 00:27:41,971
You're not leaving?

342
00:27:43,157 --> 00:27:44,250
I need to find a book.

343
00:27:44,658 --> 00:27:45,659
I see.

344
00:28:07,688 --> 00:28:08,689
Dad.

345
00:28:09,130 --> 00:28:11,530
All our distributors have pulled out of their transportation deals with us.

346
00:28:11,879 --> 00:28:12,970
They're undercutting us like crazy.

347
00:28:16,941 --> 00:28:18,290
First the port,

348
00:28:19,213 --> 00:28:20,900
now they're sticking their noses in here too?

349
00:28:22,210 --> 00:28:23,570
They started in the neighboring district.

350
00:28:24,045 --> 00:28:26,500
Now they're moving further into our territory.

351
00:28:27,168 --> 00:28:28,490
If this keeps up,

352
00:28:28,842 --> 00:28:30,650
our other businesses could be in trouble.

353
00:28:31,077 --> 00:28:32,950
You can’t let them disrespect us like this, Dad.

354
00:28:39,317 --> 00:28:40,318
Then...

355
00:28:41,669 --> 00:28:43,670
how about paying his daughter a visit?

356
00:28:45,850 --> 00:28:46,851
What?

357
00:28:48,770 --> 00:28:50,971
If you're going to take over from me,

358
00:28:51,860 --> 00:28:54,410
you need to prove you're worthy.

359
00:29:05,618 --> 00:29:06,619
Okay.

360
00:29:19,970 --> 00:29:21,390
- Hello.
- This way, please.

361
00:29:30,990 --> 00:29:31,991
Okay.

362
00:29:32,890 --> 00:29:33,891
This seat?

363
00:29:39,741 --> 00:29:40,742
What?

364
00:29:42,250 --> 00:29:44,170
You came to eat without inviting us?

365
00:29:48,210 --> 00:29:49,370
What brings you here?

366
00:29:50,050 --> 00:29:51,730
We followed you here, obviously.

367
00:29:52,080 --> 00:29:53,770
What's so weird about that? We come here all the time.

368
00:30:07,322 --> 00:30:09,300
Ooh, fish tofu with cheese!

369
00:30:23,810 --> 00:30:25,011
You don't want it?

370
00:30:26,264 --> 00:30:28,744
Nope, I want something else.

371
00:30:53,600 --> 00:30:54,601
You want some?

372
00:30:55,914 --> 00:30:56,940
Thanks.

373
00:31:08,986 --> 00:31:10,720
- Jai.
- What?

374
00:31:11,738 --> 00:31:13,592
Since when do you like cheese-filled fish tofu?

375
00:31:14,130 --> 00:31:15,810
I've always liked it, okay?

376
00:31:17,691 --> 00:31:19,210
- Yeah?
- Yeah.

377
00:31:22,674 --> 00:31:25,690
Hey, if you're not gonna eat it, why are you taking it from me?

378
00:31:25,760 --> 00:31:28,410
I wasn't taking it from you. I was gonna feed you.

379
00:31:28,533 --> 00:31:30,370
- Hey, it's still hot.
- Eat it while it's hot.

380
00:31:35,858 --> 00:31:36,859
Is it good?

381
00:31:38,970 --> 00:31:40,170
Damn! It's too hot.

382
00:31:59,504 --> 00:32:00,505
What are you doing?

383
00:32:01,090 --> 00:32:03,030
I'm just stiff. I was stretching.

384
00:32:25,498 --> 00:32:27,531
Hey, I'll be right back.

385
00:32:28,336 --> 00:32:30,485
- Where are you going?
- I'm going to get some Tokyo pancakes.

386
00:32:31,194 --> 00:32:32,195
I'll be right back.

387
00:32:43,381 --> 00:32:45,610
Two custard-filled pancakes, please.

388
00:33:11,850 --> 00:33:14,450
[Tokyo: Sorry. I'll find a way to send those two home ASAP.]

389
00:33:16,970 --> 00:33:18,490
[Blue: It's okay. We can go on a date another day.]

390
00:33:23,450 --> 00:33:24,770
[Tokyo: Okay. I'll bring you some custard-filled pancakes.]

391
00:33:47,230 --> 00:33:50,410
A Monchaitrakul shouldn't be out here like this.

392
00:33:57,410 --> 00:33:58,411
Don't you know it's dangerous?

393
00:34:01,245 --> 00:34:02,410
Dangerous how?

394
00:34:02,970 --> 00:34:03,971
Come on.

395
00:34:04,610 --> 00:34:06,650
Because everyone in this town is with the Kongpurims.

396
00:34:12,170 --> 00:34:13,171
Then

397
00:34:13,650 --> 00:34:15,490
how come people are still working at the port

398
00:34:15,845 --> 00:34:17,050
like nothing's changed?

399
00:34:18,485 --> 00:34:20,930
- You dare talk back to the boss? Huh?
- Hey!

400
00:34:21,490 --> 00:34:23,530
Can you really hurt a girl?

401
00:34:31,362 --> 00:34:33,350
We usually leave girls alone.

402
00:34:34,530 --> 00:34:36,250
But when it comes to the Monchaitrakuls,

403
00:34:37,210 --> 00:34:38,330
no one's getting spared.

404
00:34:39,070 --> 00:34:40,350
Not even women or children.

405
00:34:48,020 --> 00:34:49,021
Hey.

406
00:34:49,845 --> 00:34:50,846
Hi.

407
00:34:51,930 --> 00:34:53,050
You're eating here too?

408
00:34:56,333 --> 00:34:58,290
No. I'm here to collect the interest.

409
00:34:59,354 --> 00:35:01,355
Who are you here with?

410
00:35:16,678 --> 00:35:18,010
With Jai and Pupay, of course.

411
00:35:21,150 --> 00:35:22,151
Yeah?

412
00:35:29,141 --> 00:35:30,142
Yeah.

413
00:35:51,736 --> 00:35:52,770
What did you do?

414
00:35:56,167 --> 00:35:57,610
I burned my hand on an iron.

415
00:36:00,310 --> 00:36:01,311
I told you,

416
00:36:01,495 --> 00:36:03,757
getting mixed up with the Kongpurims is nothing but trouble..

417
00:36:05,240 --> 00:36:06,570
If that burn doesn't heal,

418
00:36:07,218 --> 00:36:08,530
you'd better see a doctor soon.

419
00:36:09,234 --> 00:36:11,050
We're visiting my dad's grave soon.

420
00:36:11,346 --> 00:36:13,410
If your dad sees your hand like that, he'll get mad again

421
00:36:14,658 --> 00:36:15,659
Oh, right.

422
00:36:16,632 --> 00:36:18,370
Your dad's death anniversary is coming up.

423
00:36:21,633 --> 00:36:25,050
Next time, come up with a better lie.

424
00:36:25,650 --> 00:36:28,975
That's not a burn from an iron. I'm not that stupid.

425
00:36:31,066 --> 00:36:33,210
Besides, now that you've moved here,

426
00:36:33,807 --> 00:36:36,750
I'm all you've got so let me help you.

427
00:36:39,375 --> 00:36:41,130
You don't have to keep things from me.

428
00:36:46,706 --> 00:36:49,490
Are you free tomorrow?

429
00:37:16,850 --> 00:37:17,851
What is going on?

430
00:37:19,128 --> 00:37:20,129
You brought me here for a fight?

431
00:37:21,981 --> 00:37:24,530
- Should've brought more backup.
- Nope.

432
00:37:36,024 --> 00:37:37,090
(In unison) We're dating.

433
00:37:41,090 --> 00:37:42,770
I'd rather you called me here for a fight.

434
00:37:48,157 --> 00:37:49,210
I need to ask you this:

435
00:37:49,941 --> 00:37:52,450
do you really think two people from rival mafia families in this province

436
00:37:52,730 --> 00:37:54,210
could ever make a relationship work?

437
00:37:54,970 --> 00:37:56,210
You think it's gonna last?

438
00:37:57,890 --> 00:37:59,989
We're trying.

439
00:38:02,565 --> 00:38:04,110
As for whether we'll last,

440
00:38:04,933 --> 00:38:06,770
can we at least give it a shot?

441
00:38:11,930 --> 00:38:12,931
Sure.

442
00:38:15,097 --> 00:38:18,010
You've already made up your minds. What are you asking me for?

443
00:38:21,645 --> 00:38:23,110
Then you two have to promise me

444
00:38:23,746 --> 00:38:26,730
you'll tell me if anything happens.

445
00:38:31,453 --> 00:38:32,454
I'm worried about you.

446
00:38:34,904 --> 00:38:35,905
I promise.

447
00:38:36,872 --> 00:38:38,373
I'll tell you first if anything happens,

448
00:38:39,410 --> 00:38:40,411
okay?

449
00:38:44,165 --> 00:38:45,166
You promise?

450
00:38:46,290 --> 00:38:47,930
I promise.

451
00:38:52,762 --> 00:38:53,763
So this is why

452
00:38:54,896 --> 00:38:56,897
you don't want to move out of the dorm and live with your dad, huh?

453
00:38:59,550 --> 00:39:00,551
Yeah.

454
00:39:08,359 --> 00:39:09,360
Hey.

455
00:39:11,930 --> 00:39:13,290
[Pakkard, please don't be mad.]

456
00:39:19,186 --> 00:39:20,187
Just take it.

457
00:39:26,146 --> 00:39:27,650
"Pakkard, please don't be mad."

458
00:40:08,730 --> 00:40:11,450
My mouth's messy too. How about wiping mine?

459
00:40:23,610 --> 00:40:25,811
[Tokyo: Don't forget to put ointment on your wound so it'll heal faster.]

460
00:40:25,930 --> 00:40:27,931
[Blue: Pakkard already helped me with that.]

461
00:40:27,940 --> 00:40:29,418
If the Monchaitrakuls keep this up,

462
00:40:33,250 --> 00:40:35,610
we'll have to handle it the same way we did 17 years ago.

463
00:40:40,637 --> 00:40:41,638
It's okay.

464
00:40:42,429 --> 00:40:43,450
I will handle this.

465
00:40:44,733 --> 00:40:47,410
All you need to do is clean up afterward.

466
00:40:52,874 --> 00:40:53,875
Got it.

467
00:41:09,950 --> 00:41:11,570
You can't even take care of yourself

468
00:41:12,613 --> 00:41:14,010
and we're worried about you.

469
00:41:14,565 --> 00:41:16,350
How can we let you out of our sight?

470
00:41:17,630 --> 00:41:18,631
Sure I can.

471
00:41:18,989 --> 00:41:20,350
I'm not a little girl anymore.

472
00:41:21,950 --> 00:41:25,610
If you're still acting on impulse and can't even support yourself,

473
00:41:26,461 --> 00:41:27,750
you're not grown up yet, sweetheart.

474
00:41:33,621 --> 00:41:34,650
Tell me honestly.

475
00:41:37,071 --> 00:41:39,130
Why don't you want to move back home with me?

476
00:41:52,757 --> 00:41:53,770
Are you seeing someone?

477
00:41:59,850 --> 00:42:02,750
I don't mind if you are.

478
00:42:03,941 --> 00:42:06,090
You can date with us around, sweetheart.

479
00:42:06,816 --> 00:42:10,150
Whether it's a girl or a boy, it's perfectly normal. I understand that.

480
00:42:10,597 --> 00:42:12,498
It's not about that, Mom.

481
00:42:14,613 --> 00:42:16,050
I can handle it myself.

482
00:42:27,565 --> 00:42:29,170
Or is the reason you can't tell me

483
00:42:32,082 --> 00:42:33,370
that they're a Kongpurim?

484
00:42:57,250 --> 00:42:59,410
[The accident 17 years ago]

485
00:43:09,869 --> 00:43:10,870
Mom.

486
00:43:11,754 --> 00:43:13,350
Mom, please don't tell Dad.

487
00:43:14,210 --> 00:43:16,170
I don't want things to get any more complicated.

488
00:43:17,290 --> 00:43:18,291
Blue,

489
00:43:18,930 --> 00:43:22,010
your dad isn't being unreasonable

490
00:43:22,031 --> 00:43:23,850
or just holding some senseless grudge.

491
00:43:26,149 --> 00:43:27,650
Someone actually died

492
00:43:28,330 --> 00:43:30,731
because of the feud between our two families,

493
00:43:32,331 --> 00:43:35,210
Uncle Wirat, Pakkarn's father.

494
00:43:36,490 --> 00:43:39,791
[A Businessman, Wirat, brutally murdered in a luxury car]

495
00:43:43,394 --> 00:43:46,090
We have proof,

496
00:43:48,034 --> 00:43:50,490
but they've got powerful people behind them.

497
00:43:51,533 --> 00:43:53,370
That's why we can't get justice.

498
00:43:57,725 --> 00:43:58,850
You understand

499
00:44:00,402 --> 00:44:03,150
this is more than just kids' stuff now, don't you, sweetheart?

500
00:44:14,773 --> 00:44:16,250
I'll talk to your dad

501
00:44:17,090 --> 00:44:19,410
about letting you stay at the dorm.

502
00:44:22,586 --> 00:44:23,587
Blue,

503
00:44:25,877 --> 00:44:28,090
you have to cut ties with that family.

504
00:44:30,544 --> 00:44:31,545
For your own good.

505
00:44:39,167 --> 00:44:40,168
I should go.

506
00:44:48,613 --> 00:44:50,370
Maybe leaving together

507
00:44:51,861 --> 00:44:53,410
could be the answer for both of us.

508
00:44:56,741 --> 00:44:58,350
Are you sure about going away with me?

509
00:45:00,266 --> 00:45:01,267
Yes, I'm sure.

510
00:45:46,610 --> 00:45:49,450
[Can you come meet me at Auntie's stall by the pier?]

511
00:45:56,319 --> 00:45:57,320
Do you think

512
00:45:58,501 --> 00:46:00,380
what my mom said is true?

513
00:46:03,010 --> 00:46:06,320
I don't know. True or made up, who gives a shit?

514
00:46:07,952 --> 00:46:08,953
Why's that?

515
00:46:10,581 --> 00:46:11,582
Be honest.

516
00:46:12,309 --> 00:46:14,757
You don't have to spare my feelings just because I'm dating Tokyo.

517
00:46:16,405 --> 00:46:18,100
I'm not trying to comfort you.

518
00:46:18,690 --> 00:46:21,391
There's no clear proof the Kongpurims did it.

519
00:46:22,330 --> 00:46:24,450
Both sides tell the story to make themselves look good.

520
00:46:27,899 --> 00:46:31,050
What is your side of the story?

521
00:46:34,160 --> 00:46:35,550
The truth from my side?

522
00:46:36,161 --> 00:46:38,666
After my dad died,

523
00:46:39,125 --> 00:46:41,850
I've been living here with relatives on my mom's side

524
00:46:43,213 --> 00:46:44,570
The Kongpurims have paid for my education

525
00:46:45,100 --> 00:46:47,250
through scholarships ever since I was a kid.

526
00:46:47,834 --> 00:46:50,435
And they've never treated people in the community badly.

527
00:46:51,010 --> 00:46:53,400
Do you really expect me to believe they're bad people?

528
00:46:58,290 --> 00:47:00,170
Honestly,

529
00:47:01,397 --> 00:47:04,370
I don't care about what happened in the past.

530
00:47:05,226 --> 00:47:06,450
What matters to me is today.

531
00:47:07,298 --> 00:47:09,330
If they're not treating you badly now,

532
00:47:10,045 --> 00:47:11,390
then I still believe in them.

533
00:47:21,941 --> 00:47:23,490
There's something that can't wait.

534
00:47:23,962 --> 00:47:26,763
I want to talk to you about it right now.

535
00:47:29,666 --> 00:47:31,137
You already knew about this, didn't you?

536
00:47:32,290 --> 00:47:33,291
About…

537
00:47:34,685 --> 00:47:36,925
Your uncle who died 17 years ago.

538
00:47:45,202 --> 00:47:46,970
Honestly, I'm not sure

539
00:47:47,469 --> 00:47:49,170
about what happened either.

540
00:47:49,925 --> 00:47:51,710
I'm not sure if my family did it.

541
00:48:00,000 --> 00:48:01,001
But …

542
00:48:02,801 --> 00:48:04,050
I understand

543
00:48:04,752 --> 00:48:06,810
if you don't want to be with me.

544
00:48:08,768 --> 00:48:11,130
What happened was really terrible.

545
00:48:15,482 --> 00:48:18,312
Once I find proof that

546
00:48:18,813 --> 00:48:20,877
the Kongpurims weren't responsible,

547
00:48:22,552 --> 00:48:25,490
- we can get back together then.
- I don't care about any of that.

548
00:48:28,797 --> 00:48:32,110
Why should we have to inherit a feud the adults started?

549
00:48:38,165 --> 00:48:39,166
Besides,

550
00:48:41,647 --> 00:48:43,090
I like you.

551
00:48:45,541 --> 00:48:47,250
I have no reason to stop seeing you.

552
00:48:56,618 --> 00:48:58,050
You really believe that?

553
00:48:58,960 --> 00:48:59,961
Yeah.

554
00:49:02,810 --> 00:49:04,530
They made this mess.

555
00:49:05,968 --> 00:49:07,380
Let them deal with it.

556
00:50:21,960 --> 00:50:23,470
- [Next Episode Preview]
- This is Tong.

557
00:50:23,750 --> 00:50:26,730
representing Sappakan Sueksa. Why don't you get to know each other?

558
00:50:27,251 --> 00:50:28,600
Tong invited me to take art classes with him.

559
00:50:28,950 --> 00:50:30,450
Your ex?

560
00:50:32,538 --> 00:50:36,139
Tokyo, you're not dating that family's daughter, are you?

561
00:50:37,296 --> 00:50:39,450
I won't let it go for sure.

562
00:50:39,925 --> 00:50:41,250
You're putting Blue in a difficult position.

563
00:50:41,578 --> 00:50:43,010
If you truly want what's best for her,

564
00:50:43,530 --> 00:50:44,531
let her go.

